module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.AffineChart
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.EffectiveCartier
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Flatness.StalkIdealSheaf
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Groupoids.IdealSheafComap

/-!
# The exceptional ideal of a blowup on an affine chart

Let `S` be a scheme, `ℐ` a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals on `S` and `b : X' ⟶ S` the blowup of
`S` in `ℐ`. For an affine open `U ⊆ S` and a section `a ∈ ℐ(U)` the chart
`Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart` identifies an affine open of `X'` with the spectrum of the
affine blowup algebra `Γ(S, U)[ℐ(U)/a]`; those charts cover `b⁻¹(U)` by the second assertion of
Stacks tag 0804.

This file computes the exceptional ideal `ℐ·𝒪_{X'}` on such a chart. Two steps:

* the composite `Spec Γ(S, U)[ℐ(U)/a] ⟶ X' ⟶ S` is `Spec` of the structure map of the affine
  blowup algebra, followed by the affine identification of `U`
  (`Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart_blowUpToBase`);
* hence the inverse-image ideal on the chart is the ideal generated by the image of `ℐ(U)`,
  which is generated by the image of `a` and that image is a nonzerodivisor
  (`Stacks.Blowup.ideal_comap_exceptionalIdeal_blowUpAffineChart`).

Together with the covering statement this gives the first half of the second assertion of Stacks
tag 02OS: the exceptional divisor of a blowup is a locally principal closed subscheme, cut out
locally by a single nonzerodivisor. The remaining half — that the ideal *sheaf* is an invertible
`𝒪_{X'}`-module, which is how `Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor` is phrased — is not
proved here; see the implementation notes.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart_blowUpToBase`: the affine chart of the blowup attached to
  `a ∈ ℐ(U)`, composed with the blowup morphism, is `Spec` of the structure map
  `Γ(S, U) ⟶ Γ(S, U)[ℐ(U)/a]` followed by `Γ(S, U)`'s affine identification with `U`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.ideal_comap_exceptionalIdeal_blowUpAffineChart`: the inverse image of the
  exceptional ideal on the chart `Spec Γ(S, U)[ℐ(U)/a]` is generated by the image of `a`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalChartSection`: the generator, as a section of the structure sheaf of
  `X'` over the affine open underlying that chart.
* `Stacks.Blowup.ideal_exceptionalIdeal_blowUpAffineChart` and
  `Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalChartSection_mem_nonZeroDivisors`: on that affine open the
  exceptional ideal is generated by that section, and the section is a nonzerodivisor.
* `Stacks.Blowup.exists_span_eq_ideal_exceptionalIdeal_blowUpAffineChart`: on the affine open of
  `X'` underlying that chart the exceptional ideal is generated by a single nonzerodivisor.
* `Stacks.Blowup.isLocallyPrincipal_exceptionalIdeal`: the exceptional divisor of a blowup is a
  locally principal closed subscheme.
* `Stacks.Blowup.ideal_comap_fromSpec_top`: the inverse-image ideal sheaf on affine opens, for
  the affine identification of an affine open.

## Implementation notes

`Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor` is the invertibility of the ideal sheaf as a sheaf of
modules (`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible`, the "tensoring is an equivalence" form
of Stacks tag 01CS), so deducing it from the local data proved here needs the forward half of
Stacks tag 01WS. The note in `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Divisors/EffectiveCartier.lean`
saying that this passes through "an invertible sheaf of modules is locally free of rank one" is
about the *converse* direction; for the direction needed here the route is the dual-pairing
criterion `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isInvertible_of_dualBasisOne` in
`StacksFrontier/Algebra/Category/ModuleCat/Sheaf/SheafHom.lean`, whose remaining input is the
conversion of a rank-one local trivialization into a `Stacks.SheafOfModules.DualBasisOne`.

Three elaboration points, all instances of the rule that an instantiated conclusion in this area
must be inferred rather than written out. The factorization of the chart over the base is proved
by rewriting at the level of `Proj.awayι_toSpecZero_assoc`, with the affine identification of `U`
spelled through `Stacks.RelativeProj.isAffineOpen` rather than `U.2` — the latter elaborates as a
membership in `S.affineOpens` instead of as `IsAffineOpen`, and the resulting goal is not
type-correct at `implicit` transparency. Assembling the inverse-image computation by `rw` on the
`Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap` chain exhausts the heartbeat budget, while the same composition
built from `congrArg` against lemmas whose types are inferred costs nothing. And the purely
ring-theoretic step comparing `Spec`'s global sections with the ring map is isolated as
`Stacks.Blowup.map_appTop_map_ΓSpecIso_inv`, with both rings behind variables, because
`← CommRingCat.hom_comp` against the written-out conclusion times out.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0804](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0804)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OS)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Limits CommRingCat

universe u

namespace Stacks.Blowup

/-! ### Inverse-image ideal sheaves on affine opens -/

/-- Comapping an ideal along the inverse of a ring isomorphism is mapping it along the
isomorphism. -/
theorem comap_inv_eq_map_hom {A B : CommRingCat.{u}} (e : A ≅ B) (J : Ideal A) :
    J.comap e.inv.hom = J.map e.hom.hom :=
  Ideal.comap_symm (I := J) e.commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv

/-- Transporting a `Spec`-level ideal through the global sections of `Spec`: mapping along the
global sections of `Spec φ` after the canonical identification agrees with mapping along `φ`
first. -/
theorem map_appTop_map_ΓSpecIso_inv {R T : CommRingCat.{u}} (g : R ⟶ T) (J : Ideal R) :
    Ideal.map ((Spec.map g).appTop).hom (Ideal.map ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso R).inv).hom J)
      = Ideal.map ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso T).inv).hom (Ideal.map g.hom J) := by
  rw [Ideal.map_map, Ideal.map_map, ← CommRingCat.hom_comp, ← CommRingCat.hom_comp,
    Scheme.ΓSpecIso_inv_naturality]

/-- The inverse image of an ideal sheaf along an open immersion, on an affine open, is the image
of the ideal of the image affine open under the section isomorphism. -/
private theorem ideal_comap_eq_map_appIso_hom {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (I : Y.IdealSheafData)
    (f : X ⟶ Y) [IsOpenImmersion f] (U : X.affineOpens) :
    (I.comap f).ideal U
      = Ideal.map (f.appIso U).hom.hom (I.ideal ⟨f ''ᵁ U, U.2.image_of_isOpenImmersion f⟩) := by
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_comap_of_isOpenImmersion, comap_inv_eq_map_hom]

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} (ℐ : S.IdealSheafData)

/-- **The inverse image of an ideal sheaf under the affine identification of an affine open.**
Read on `Spec Γ(S, U)` it is the ideal `ℐ(U)`. -/
theorem ideal_comap_fromSpec_top (U : S.affineOpens) :
    (ℐ.comap (Stacks.RelativeProj.isAffineOpen U).fromSpec).ideal
        ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩
      = Ideal.map ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso Γ(S, U.1)).inv).hom (ℐ.ideal U) := by
  have hV : ((Stacks.RelativeProj.isAffineOpen U).fromSpec ''ᵁ
      (⊤ : (Spec Γ(S, U.1)).Opens)) ≤ (U : S.Opens) :=
    ((Stacks.RelativeProj.isAffineOpen U).opensRange_fromSpec ▸
      Scheme.Hom.image_top_eq_opensRange _).le
  have hρ : S.presheaf.map (homOfLE hV).op ≫
        ((Stacks.RelativeProj.isAffineOpen U).fromSpec.appIso
          (⊤ : (Spec Γ(S, U.1)).Opens)).hom
      = (Scheme.ΓSpecIso Γ(S, U.1)).inv := by
    rw [Scheme.Hom.appIso_hom', Scheme.Hom.map_appLE]
    simp only [Scheme.Hom.appLE, (Stacks.RelativeProj.isAffineOpen U).fromSpec_app_self,
      Category.assoc, ← Functor.map_comp, ← op_comp]
    simp
  have h1 := ideal_comap_eq_map_appIso_hom ℐ (Stacks.RelativeProj.isAffineOpen U).fromSpec
      ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩
  have h2 := ℐ.map_ideal (U := ⟨_, (isAffineOpen_top (Spec Γ(S, U.1))).image_of_isOpenImmersion
      (Stacks.RelativeProj.isAffineOpen U).fromSpec⟩) (V := U) hV
  rw [h1, ← h2, Ideal.map_map]
  exact congrArg (fun φ : Γ(S, U.1) ⟶ _ => Ideal.map φ.hom (ℐ.ideal U)) hρ

/-! ### The affine chart of a blowup over its base -/

/-- The chart of the blowup over an affine open `U`, composed with the blowup morphism, is the
structure morphism of the chart followed by the inclusion of `U`. -/
theorem blowUpChart_blowUpToBase (U : S.affineOpens) :
    blowUpChart ℐ U ≫ blowUpToBase ℐ =
      Stacks.RelativeProj.chartToOpen (fun W : S.affineOpens ↦ reesGrading (ℐ.ideal W)) U
        (reesBase ℐ U) ≫ U.1.ι :=
  (reesData ℐ).chartι_toBase U

/-- The structure map of the chart `(Γ(S, U)[ℐ(U)t])_{(a⁽¹⁾)}` over the degree-zero part of the
Rees algebra corresponds, under the chart identification with the affine blowup algebra, to the
structure map `Γ(S, U) ⟶ Γ(S, U)[ℐ(U)/a]`.

This is `Stacks.Blowup.reesAwayEquivAffineBlowup_fromZeroRingHom` composed with
`Stacks.Blowup.reesBase`, stated as an equality of morphisms of `CommRingCat`. -/
theorem reesBase_fromZeroRingHom_reesAwayEquivAffineBlowup (U : S.affineOpens)
    {a : Γ(S, U.1)} (ha : a ∈ ℐ.ideal U) :
    reesBase ℐ U ≫ CommRingCat.ofHom
        (HomogeneousLocalization.fromZeroRingHom (reesGrading (ℐ.ideal U))
          (Submonoid.powers (reesDegOne (ℐ.ideal U) ha))) ≫
        (reesAwayEquivAffineBlowup (ℐ.ideal U) a ha).toCommRingCatIso.hom
      = CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap Γ(S, U.1) (affineBlowup (ℐ.ideal U) a)) := by
  refine CommRingCat.hom_ext (RingHom.ext fun z => ?_)
  have h := reesAwayEquivAffineBlowup_fromZeroRingHom (ℐ.ideal U) a ha ((reesBase ℐ U).hom z)
  change (reesAwayEquivAffineBlowup (ℐ.ideal U) a ha)
      (HomogeneousLocalization.fromZeroRingHom _ _ ((reesBase ℐ U).hom z)) = _
  rw [h]
  congr 1
  apply (reesGradingZeroEquiv (ℐ.ideal U)).injective
  rw [RingEquiv.apply_symm_apply, reesGradingZeroEquiv_apply]
  rfl

/-- **The affine chart of a blowup, over the base.** The composite
`Spec Γ(S, U)[ℐ(U)/a] ⟶ X' ⟶ S` is `Spec` of the structure map of the affine blowup algebra,
followed by the identification of `Spec Γ(S, U)` with the affine open `U`.

This is the compatibility of the chart identification of Stacks tag 0804 with the structure
morphism of the blowup; it is what reduces the exceptional ideal on a chart to the ideal
`ℐ(U)·Γ(S, U)[ℐ(U)/a]` of commutative algebra. -/
theorem blowUpAffineChart_blowUpToBase (U : S.affineOpens) {a : Γ(S, U.1)}
    (ha : a ∈ ℐ.ideal U) :
    blowUpAffineChart ℐ U ha ≫ blowUpToBase ℐ
      = Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap Γ(S, U.1) (affineBlowup (ℐ.ideal U) a)))
          ≫ (Stacks.RelativeProj.isAffineOpen U).fromSpec := by
  rw [blowUpAffineChart, Category.assoc, blowUpChart_blowUpToBase,
    Stacks.RelativeProj.chartToOpen, specAffineBlowupι]
  simp only [Category.assoc]
  rw [Proj.awayι_toSpecZero_assoc, (Stacks.RelativeProj.isAffineOpen U).isoSpec_inv_ι,
    ← Spec.map_comp_assoc, ← Spec.map_comp_assoc,
    reesBase_fromZeroRingHom_reesAwayEquivAffineBlowup]

/-! ### The exceptional ideal on an affine chart -/

/-- **The exceptional ideal, read on the chart `Spec Γ(S, U)[ℐ(U)/a]`, is generated by the image
of `a`.** This is the computation `ℐ(U)·Γ(S, U)[ℐ(U)/a] = a·Γ(S, U)[ℐ(U)/a]` of Stacks tag
07Z3 (2), transported to the chart of the blowup through
`Stacks.Blowup.blowUpAffineChart_blowUpToBase`. -/
theorem ideal_comap_exceptionalIdeal_blowUpAffineChart (U : S.affineOpens) {a : Γ(S, U.1)}
    (ha : a ∈ ℐ.ideal U) :
    ((exceptionalIdeal ℐ).comap (blowUpAffineChart ℐ U ha)).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩
      = Ideal.span {((Scheme.ΓSpecIso
            (CommRingCat.of (affineBlowup (ℐ.ideal U) a))).inv.hom
          (algebraMap Γ(S, U.1) (affineBlowup (ℐ.ideal U) a) a))} := by
  have h0 := Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap_comp ℐ (blowUpAffineChart ℐ U ha) (blowUpToBase ℐ)
  have h1 := congrArg (fun f : Spec (CommRingCat.of (affineBlowup (ℐ.ideal U) a)) ⟶ S =>
    ℐ.comap f) (blowUpAffineChart_blowUpToBase ℐ U ha)
  have h2 := Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap_comp ℐ
    (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap Γ(S, U.1) (affineBlowup (ℐ.ideal U) a))))
    (Stacks.RelativeProj.isAffineOpen U).fromSpec
  have hgoal := congrArg
    (fun J : (Spec (CommRingCat.of (affineBlowup (ℐ.ideal U) a))).IdealSheafData =>
      J.ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩) (h0.symm.trans (h1.trans h2))
  have hA := Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_top_of_isAffine
    (ℐ.comap (Stacks.RelativeProj.isAffineOpen U).fromSpec)
    (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap Γ(S, U.1) (affineBlowup (ℐ.ideal U) a))))
  have hB := congrArg
    (fun J : Ideal Γ(Spec Γ(S, U.1), ⊤) =>
      Ideal.map ((Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
        (algebraMap Γ(S, U.1) (affineBlowup (ℐ.ideal U) a)))).appTop).hom J)
    (ideal_comap_fromSpec_top ℐ U)
  have hC := map_appTop_map_ΓSpecIso_inv
    (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap Γ(S, U.1) (affineBlowup (ℐ.ideal U) a))) (ℐ.ideal U)
  have hD := congrArg
    (fun J : Ideal (affineBlowup (ℐ.ideal U) a) =>
      Ideal.map ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso
        (CommRingCat.of (affineBlowup (ℐ.ideal U) a))).inv).hom J)
    (affineBlowup_idealMap_eq_span (ℐ.ideal U) a ha)
  refine hgoal.trans (hA.trans (hB.trans (hC.trans (hD.trans ?_))))
  rw [Ideal.map_span]
  simp

/-- A nonzerodivisor stays one under a ring isomorphism. -/
theorem mem_nonZeroDivisors_iso {A B : CommRingCat.{u}} (e : A ≅ B) {t : A}
    (ht : t ∈ nonZeroDivisors A) : e.hom.hom t ∈ nonZeroDivisors B := by
  rw [← MulEquivClass.map_nonZeroDivisors e.commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv]
  exact ⟨t, ht, rfl⟩

/-- **The generator of the exceptional ideal on an affine chart of the blowup.** On the affine
open of `X'` underlying the chart `Spec Γ(S, U)[ℐ(U)/a]`, this is the image of `a` in the affine
blowup algebra, read as a section of the structure sheaf through the chart. -/
def exceptionalChartSection (U : S.affineOpens) {a : Γ(S, U.1)} (ha : a ∈ ℐ.ideal U) :
    Γ(blowUp ℐ, blowUpAffineChart ℐ U ha ''ᵁ ⊤) :=
  (((blowUpAffineChart ℐ U ha).appIso
        (⊤ : (Spec (CommRingCat.of (affineBlowup (ℐ.ideal U) a))).Opens)).inv).hom
    ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of (affineBlowup (ℐ.ideal U) a))).inv.hom
      (algebraMap Γ(S, U.1) (affineBlowup (ℐ.ideal U) a) a))

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 02OS, second assertion, affine-local form.** On the affine open of the
blowup underlying the chart `Spec Γ(S, U)[ℐ(U)/a]`, the exceptional ideal is generated by
`Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalChartSection`.

This is the equation `IA' = aA'` of the proof of Stacks tag 02OS, for the chart supplied by the
second assertion of Stacks tag 0804, transported from
`Stacks.Blowup.ideal_comap_exceptionalIdeal_blowUpAffineChart` across the chart's identification
of sections. -/
@[stacks 02OS "the exceptional ideal is generated by one section on an affine chart"]
theorem ideal_exceptionalIdeal_blowUpAffineChart (U : S.affineOpens)
    {a : Γ(S, U.1)} (ha : a ∈ ℐ.ideal U) :
    (exceptionalIdeal ℐ).ideal ⟨blowUpAffineChart ℐ U ha ''ᵁ ⊤,
        (isAffineOpen_top _).image_of_isOpenImmersion _⟩ =
      Ideal.span {exceptionalChartSection ℐ U ha} := by
  have h1 := ideal_comap_eq_map_appIso_hom (exceptionalIdeal ℐ) (blowUpAffineChart ℐ U ha)
    ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩
  have h2 := ideal_comap_exceptionalIdeal_blowUpAffineChart ℐ U ha
  have h5 := congrArg
    (fun J => Ideal.map (((blowUpAffineChart ℐ U ha).appIso (⊤ : (Spec (CommRingCat.of
      (affineBlowup (ℐ.ideal U) a))).Opens)).inv).hom J)
    (h1.symm.trans h2)
  simp only [Ideal.map_map, ← CommRingCat.hom_comp, Iso.hom_inv_id, CommRingCat.hom_id,
    Ideal.map_id, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton] at h5
  exact h5

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 02OS, second assertion, affine-local form.** The generator of the
exceptional ideal on an affine chart of the blowup is a nonzerodivisor.

This is the sentence "`a` maps to a nonzerodivisor in `A'`" of the proof of Stacks tag 02OS. -/
@[stacks 02OS "the generator on an affine chart is a nonzerodivisor"]
theorem exceptionalChartSection_mem_nonZeroDivisors (U : S.affineOpens)
    {a : Γ(S, U.1)} (ha : a ∈ ℐ.ideal U) :
    exceptionalChartSection ℐ U ha ∈
      nonZeroDivisors Γ(blowUp ℐ, blowUpAffineChart ℐ U ha ''ᵁ ⊤) :=
  mem_nonZeroDivisors_iso
    ((blowUpAffineChart ℐ U ha).appIso (⊤ : (Spec (CommRingCat.of
      (affineBlowup (ℐ.ideal U) a))).Opens)).symm
    (mem_nonZeroDivisors_iso
      (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of (affineBlowup (ℐ.ideal U) a))).symm
      (algebraMap_affineBlowup_mem_nonZeroDivisors (ℐ.ideal U) a))

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 02OS, second assertion, affine-local form.** On the affine open of the
blowup underlying the chart `Spec Γ(S, U)[ℐ(U)/a]`, the exceptional ideal is generated by a
single section, and that section is a nonzerodivisor.

This is the sentence "Then `IA' = aA'` and `a` maps to a nonzerodivisor in `A'`" of the proof of
Stacks tag 02OS, for the chart supplied by the second assertion of Stacks tag 0804. The generator
is `Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalChartSection`. -/
@[stacks 02OS "the exceptional ideal is generated by a nonzerodivisor on an affine chart"]
theorem exists_span_eq_ideal_exceptionalIdeal_blowUpAffineChart (U : S.affineOpens)
    {a : Γ(S, U.1)} (ha : a ∈ ℐ.ideal U) :
    ∃ t ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ(blowUp ℐ, blowUpAffineChart ℐ U ha ''ᵁ ⊤),
      (exceptionalIdeal ℐ).ideal ⟨blowUpAffineChart ℐ U ha ''ᵁ ⊤,
          (isAffineOpen_top _).image_of_isOpenImmersion _⟩ = Ideal.span {t} :=
  ⟨exceptionalChartSection ℐ U ha, exceptionalChartSection_mem_nonZeroDivisors ℐ U ha,
    ideal_exceptionalIdeal_blowUpAffineChart ℐ U ha⟩

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 02OS, second assertion, local principality.** The exceptional divisor
of the blowup of a scheme in a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals is a locally principal closed
subscheme: around every point of the blowup there is an affine open on which the exceptional
ideal is generated by one element.

Every point of the blowup lies over an affine open `U` of the base, hence in one of the charts
`Spec Γ(S, U)[ℐ(U)/a]` by the second assertion of Stacks tag 0804
(`Stacks.Blowup.iSup_opensRange_blowUpAffineChart`), and on that chart the exceptional ideal is
principal by `Stacks.Blowup.exists_span_eq_ideal_exceptionalIdeal_blowUpAffineChart`. -/
@[stacks 02OS "the exceptional divisor is a locally principal closed subscheme"]
theorem isLocallyPrincipal_exceptionalIdeal :
    Stacks.Divisors.IsLocallyPrincipal (exceptionalIdeal ℐ) := by
  intro x
  obtain ⟨U, hU⟩ := Stacks.Divisors.exists_affineOpens_mem ((blowUpToBase ℐ).base x)
  have hmem : x ∈ blowUpToBase ℐ ⁻¹ᵁ (U : S.Opens) := hU
  rw [← iSup_opensRange_blowUpAffineChart ℐ U, TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup] at hmem
  obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := hmem
  obtain ⟨t, -, ht⟩ := exists_span_eq_ideal_exceptionalIdeal_blowUpAffineChart ℐ U r.2
  have hx : x ∈ (blowUpAffineChart ℐ U r.2 ''ᵁ ⊤ : (blowUp ℐ).Opens) := by
    rw [Scheme.Hom.image_top_eq_opensRange]
    exact hr
  exact ⟨⟨_, (isAffineOpen_top _).image_of_isOpenImmersion _⟩, hx, ⟨t, ht⟩⟩

end Stacks.Blowup

end
